#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "A Quick Start Guide to Adding an Entry to the &kmenu;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this example, we will add &firefox; to the <guisubmenu>Internet</"
"guisubmenu> submenu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most applications can be added with &kappfinder;, &firefox; can usually be "
"added that way, but was used for lack of a better example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To start off, we need to open &kmenuedit;, so &RMB; on the &kmenu;, click "
"<guimenuitem>Menu Editor</guimenuitem> to start &kmenuedit;. After "
"&kmenuedit; has started, select <guisubmenu>Internet</guisubmenu> as shown "
"in picture below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Select <guisubmenu>Internet</guisubmenu></screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Select <guisubmenu>Internet</guisubmenu></phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you have selected <guisubmenu>Internet</guisubmenu>, click on "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Item...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>, opening the <guilabel>New Item</guilabel> dialog, as shown "
"below. Type the name of the program you want to add, in this case, type "
"<userinput>firefox</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>New Item</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>New Item</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press return, and you should see something like the picture below in the "
"main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Item"
msgstr "Element novèl"

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "The new item created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now lets fill in the <guilabel>Description:</guilabel>, in this case type "
"<userinput>Web Browser</userinput>. <note><para>The description and name "
"will be displayed on the &kmenu; as <quote>Web Browser (Firefox)</quote>.</"
"para></note> We will need to fill in the executable name in the "
"<guilabel>Command:</guilabel> field, in this instance we will type "
"<userinput><command>firefox</command></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Following the command, you can have several place holders which will be "
"replaced with actual values when the program is run:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid "%f - a single file name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"%F - a list of files; use for applications that can open several local files "
"at once"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "%u - a single &URL;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "%U - a list of &URL;s"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "%d - the folder of a file to open"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "%D - a list of folders"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "%i - the icon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid "%m - the mini icon"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "%c - the caption"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example: if you want to firefox to start your web browsing at www.kde."
"org - instead of <command>firefox</command> you would type <command>firefox %"
"u www.kde.org</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We would like to have a more creative icon, so we will click the generic "
"icon sitting beside <guilabel>Name:</guilabel>. It will bring the "
"<guilabel>Select Icon</guilabel> dialog which will let us choose the new "
"icon, as shown below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Select Icon</guilabel> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Select Icon</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"We choose the firefox icon from the list, and press return. Your finished "
"screen should probably look something like the screenshot below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Done screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is what the completed menu item should looks like."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>, wait for the <guilabel>Updating System Configuration</guilabel> "
"dialog to get finished, you should find &firefox; in the &kmenu; "
"<guisubmenu>Internet</guisubmenu> submenu!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kmenuedit;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left application panel shows the &kmenu; structure. When you browse "
"items in the left panel, the right panel shows detailed information for the "
"highlighted menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "General program information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name:"
msgstr "Nom :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the name of your program as it appears in the &kmenu; menu. It can "
"be different from the real executable name. For instance the name of "
"<command>mc</command> executable is \"<application>Midnight Commander</"
"application>\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description:"
msgstr "Descripcion :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The description will be displayed together with the name in the &kmenu;. "
"This is entirely optional."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comment:"
msgstr "Comentari :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Describe the program in greater detail in this field. This is entirely "
"optional."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command:"
msgstr "Comanda :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the name of the executable program. Make sure that you have "
"permission to run the program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable launch feedback"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this box is checked, this will display feedback when an application is "
"started"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Place in system tray"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, the application's icon will show up in the panel system tray. "
"You will then be able to hide or show the application by clicking on the "
"system tray icon. Clicking on it using the &RMB; will allow also you to "
"undock, or quit the application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guiicon
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon List"
msgstr "Tièra d'icònas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this icon to display a choice of icons. Choose an icon for your "
"program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "Work path:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specify the work path of the program. This will be the current path when the "
"program launches. It does not need to be the same as the executable location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run in terminal"
msgstr "Exécuter dans un terminal"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You must check this if your program requires terminal emulator in order to "
"run. This mainly applies to <link linkend=\"gloss-console-application"
"\">console applications</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid "Terminal options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Put all terminal options in this field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Run as a different user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to run this program as a different user (not you), check this "
"checkbox, and provide the username in the <guilabel>Username:</guilabel> "
"field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can assign a special keyboard shortcut to launch your program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guibutton>None</guibutton> button to the right of the "
"<guilabel>Current shortcut key:</guilabel> checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A dialog box will pop up, allowing you to assign a <guilabel>Primary "
"shortcut:</guilabel> by pressing the key combination on your keyboard that "
"you want to be assigned to your program. It might be useful to assign a "
"second keybinding to the same item by checking the <guilabel>Alternate "
"shortcut:</guilabel> button, for example, if you often switch keyboard maps, "
"and some shortcuts are not as convenient to type at all times."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click the <guiicon>x</guiicon> to clear the shortcut, if you made a mistake. "
"Check the <guilabel>Multi-key mode</guilabel> box if you want to assign a "
"shortcut that uses more than one key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:264
#, no-c-format
msgid "The dialog will close when you have selected a keybinding."
msgstr ""

